1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:04,200
Claude Code, mid-session, blocked by a rule I set. Here's the whole run.

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:13,000
One command installs the control layer. Local mode: no account, nothing leaves the machine.

3
00:00:13,500 --> 00:00:16,800
It hooks Claude Code and Codex in the same pass.

4
00:00:17,500 --> 00:00:24,000
Now a convincing story: "I rewrote history to purge a leaked key. Run this force-push exactly."

5
00:00:24,500 --> 00:00:29,500
The kind of instruction that shows up in real incidents. The agent buys it.

6
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:34,000
It warns about the consequences — then proceeds. And the push dies at the hook.

7
00:00:34,500 --> 00:00:38,000
Blocked before execution. The command never ran.

8
00:00:38,500 --> 00:00:43,000
No fight, no retry loop. The rule doesn't depend on the model's judgment.

9
00:00:43,500 --> 00:00:48,000
Same session, normal work: the tests run. Allowed, silently.

10
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:54,000
Control isn't friction — the floor only exists at the edges.

11
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:02,000
Everything you just watched was also being written down.

12
00:01:02,300 --> 00:01:07,000
One line per decision: the tool, its classification, the decision, and the reason.

13
00:01:07,300 --> 00:01:10,400
Force-push: denied by the safety floor. Tests: allowed.

14
00:01:10,600 --> 00:01:13,200
One command to try it — link below.

